<title>JAPAN: Nomura Sec keeps falling on scandal impact.</title>
<headline>Nomura Sec keeps falling on scandal impact.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nomura Securities Co Ltd fell sharply to a new low for the year in heavy trade on Tuesday after a number of investment management firms suspended business with the brokerage, brokers said.</p>
<p>The customers suspended business after Nomura disclosed that two of its directors were involved in suspected illegal deals.</p>
<p>As of 0501 GMT, the shares were down 70 yen at 1,400 on turnover of 9.788 million shares, making it the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
</text>
